- Prevent cross-tenant friendships
- Ensure message ownership validation

---------------------------------
E) STATS & LEADERBOARDS
---------------------------------

Includes:
- External API ingestion (Riot, Epic, Steam, etc.)
- Account linking
- Match history caching
- ELO rating system
- Global leaderboard (per config_id)
- Game-specific leaderboards

ELO must:
- Be deterministic
- Be tenant-scoped
- Prevent manipulation

Background ingestion should:
- Handle rate limits
- Be resilient to API failures

---------------------------------
F) GAMIFICATION
---------------------------------

Includes:
- XP tracking
- Level progression
- Cosmetic unlocks
- Rarity tiers (common, rare, epic, legendary)

Rules:
- XP must be anti-abuse
- Unlocks must verify eligibility
- Cosmetics owned per user per config_id

====================================================
7) EDGE FUNCTION POLICY
====================================================

Use Edge Functions for:

- Multi-step transactional logic
- Tournament operations
- ELO recalculation
- XP reward distribution
- External API sync
- AI orchestration

All Edge Functions must:

- Validate JWT
- Resolve and enforce config_id
- Validate ownership
- Validate role
- Return structured JSON
- Be idempotent where possible
- Fail safely

Service_role allowed only inside secure backend context.

Never expose it.

====================================================
8) MIGRATION POLICY
====================================================

- One logical change per migration
- Clear naming
- Include config_id by default
- Add indexes immediately
- Add RLS policies in same migration
- Provide rollback guidance
- Avoid destructive changes without justification

Never mix frontend logic into migrations.

